4252	/// Choose the capacity for a page that `grow` is about to append after
4253	/// `last`, the page that just filled up.
4254	///
4255	/// The grid size (cols and rows) is always the standard one from
4256	/// `initialCapacity`. The other dimensions (styles, graphemes, strings,
4257	/// and hyperlinks) hold variable-size data. When a page runs out of room
4258	/// in one of them, `increaseCapacity` doubles that dimension and copies
4259	/// the whole page into a new, larger page. That copy is expensive. If
4260	/// every new page started over from the standard capacity, output with
4261	/// many styles or hyperlinks would pay for those copies again on every
4262	/// page, around ten copies per page in practice.
4263	///
4264	/// Instead, each new page starts from what recent pages used:
4265	///
4266	///   1. `utilizationCapacity` measures `last`. A dimension that was well
4267	///      used keeps its capacity, and one that was mostly empty shrinks
4268	///      back toward the standard size. See `DimensionUsage.nextCapacity`.
4269	///   2. Each dimension is raised to at least what the `grow_hint_pages`
4270	///      pages before `last` needed (`grow_hints`), as long as `last`
4271	///      still used the dimension. Usage varies from page to page even
4272	///      when the output is steady, and a few light pages should not
4273	///      throw away capacity that the next heavy page will need again.
4274	///      Random OSC 8 output, for example, puts between 700 and 10000
4275	///      linked cells on a page, and with a one-page memory about one
4276	///      page in nine shrank the hyperlink map after a light page and
4277	///      grew it again, copying the whole page, on the next heavy one.
4278	///      Remembering three pages makes that about one page in ninety.
4279	///      If `last` and the page before it used none of a dimension,
4280	///      only the page before `last` counts, so output that stops using
4281	///      a dimension gets standard pages again as quickly as before.
4282	///
4283	/// For example, suppose a program draws a few hundred unique styles on
4284	/// every screen. The first page grows its style capacity a few times.
4285	/// Every page after that starts with the larger capacity and never needs
7330	pub fn pageIterator(
7331	    self: *const PageList,
7332	    direction: Direction,
7333	    tl_pt: point.Point,
7334	    bl_pt: ?point.Point,
7335	) PageIterator {
7336	    const tl_pin = self.pin(tl_pt).?;
7337	    const bl_pin = if (bl_pt) |pt|
7338	        self.pin(pt).?
7339	    else
7340	        self.getBottomRight(tl_pt) orelse return .{ .row = null };
7341	
7342	    if (build_options.slow_runtime_safety) {
7343	        assert(tl_pin.eql(bl_pin) or tl_pin.before(bl_pin));
7344	    }
7345	
7346	    return switch (direction) {
7347	        .right_down => tl_pin.pageIterator(.right_down, bl_pin),
7348	        .left_up => bl_pin.pageIterator(.left_up, tl_pin),
7349	    };
